      "independent_solution": "Factor the equation as(x-y)(x+y)=69. Natural x,y are nonnegative, and the positive difference69 implies x>y. Thus u=x-y>0 and v=x+y>=u are positive integers with uv=69. Since69=3*23, the positive factor pairs with u<=v are(1,69) and(3,23). Both factors are odd, so x=(u+v)/2 and y=(v-u)/2 are integers. These give(x,y)=(35,34) and(13,10). Directly35^2-34^2=1225-1156=69 and13^2-10^2=169-100=69. The factor-pair list is exhaustive, so the complete set is{(13,10),(35,34)}.",
